@startuml
title Healthcare Microservices - Sequence Diagram

actor Client
participant "API Gateway" as api_gateway
participant "Auth Service" as auth_service
participant "Doctor Service" as doctor_service
participant "Patient Service" as patient_service
participant "Appointment Service" as appointment_service
database MongoDB
queue "Apache Kafka" as Kafka
participant "Notification Service" as notification_service
participant "SMTP Server" as SMTP

== Authentication Flow ==
Client -> api_gateway: POST /api/v1/auth/signin (SignIn)
api_gateway -> auth_service: Sign-In
auth_service -> MongoDB: Verify Credentials
MongoDB --> auth_service: Credentials Valid
auth_service --> api_gateway: Return JWT Token
api_gateway --> Client: Return JWT Token (200 OK)

Client -> api_gateway: POST /api/v1/auth/signup (SignUp)
api_gateway -> auth_service: Forward Sign-Up
auth_service -> MongoDB: Verify User Credentials
MongoDB --> auth_service: Create/Save User
auth_service --> api_gateway: Return JWT Token
api_gateway --> Client: Return JWT Token (200 OK)

Client -> api_gateway: POST /api/v1/auth
api_gateway -> auth_service: Forward Authentication
auth_service -> MongoDB: Verify Credentials
MongoDB --> auth_service: Credentials Valid
auth_service --> api_gateway: Return (202 ACCEPTED)
api_gateway --> Client: 202 ACCEPTED

== Business Flow: Patient Operations ==
Client -> api_gateway: GET /api/v1/patient/details
api_gateway -> auth_service: Validate JWT & RBAC
auth_service --> api_gateway: 202 ACCEPTED
api_gateway -> patient_service: Route to Patient Service
patient_service -> MongoDB: Query Patient Details
MongoDB --> patient_service: Patient Data
patient_service --> Client: Patient Details

Client -> api_gateway: POST /api/v1/appointments/create
api_gateway -> auth_service: Validate JWT & RBAC
auth_service --> api_gateway: 202 ACCEPTED
api_gateway -> appointment_service: Route to Appointment Service
appointment_service -> MongoDB: Save Appointment (PENDING)
MongoDB --> appointment_service: Acknowledged
appointment_service -> Kafka: Publish "Appointment Created" Event
appointment_service --> Client: 200 OK

Client -> api_gateway: GET /api/v1/appointments/patient/{id}
api_gateway -> auth_service: Validate JWT & RBAC
auth_service --> api_gateway: 202 ACCEPTED
api_gateway -> appointment_service: Route to Appointment Service
appointment_service -> MongoDB: Query Appointments
MongoDB --> appointment_service: Appointments List
appointment_service --> Client: Appointments List

== Business Flow: Doctor Operations ==
Client -> api_gateway: GET /api/v1/doctor/details
api_gateway -> auth_service: Validate JWT & RBAC
auth_service --> api_gateway: 202 ACCEPTED
api_gateway -> doctor_service: Route to Doctor Service
doctor_service -> MongoDB: Query Doctor Details
MongoDB --> doctor_service: Doctor Data
doctor_service --> Client: Doctor Details

Client -> api_gateway: GET /api/v1/appointments/doctor/{id}
api_gateway -> auth_service: Validate JWT & RBAC
auth_service --> api_gateway: 202 ACCEPTED
api_gateway -> appointment_service: Route to Appointment Service
appointment_service -> MongoDB: Query Appointments
MongoDB --> appointment_service: Appointments List
appointment_service --> Client: Appointments List

Client -> api_gateway: PUT /api/v1/appointments/{id}/status\n(APPROVE/REJECT)
api_gateway -> auth_service: Validate JWT & RBAC
auth_service --> api_gateway: 202 ACCEPTED
api_gateway -> appointment_service: Route to Appointment Service
appointment_service -> MongoDB: Update Appointment Status
MongoDB --> appointment_service: Acknowledged
appointment_service -> Kafka: Publish "Appointment Updated" Event
appointment_service --> Client: 200 OK

== Event-Driven Notification ==
Kafka <- notification_service: Consume Events (Created/Updated)
notification_service -> SMTP: Generate & Send Email
SMTP --> Client: Deliver Email (Confirmation/Rejection/Creation)
@enduml
